codex
The paper’s main result is existential, not an algorithmic hardness theorem: Theorem 1.4 guarantees \(k\) disjoint cycles from a degree imbalance and the maximum packing of triangles. That immediately makes the naïve planted-random-graph proposal suspect—dense random graphs usually expose many easy triangle packings—so I’m now checking the proof’s constructive content and the repository’s required baseline attacks before choosing a track.
